WEBVTT

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:57.700
The first-ever World Riding 
Duel Grand Prix finally begins!

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:27.300
Every time you're hurt, you can become kinder

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:32.840
Stand up and you'll understand strength

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:37.420
Don't look back and keep going

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:43.080
Both the past and the future 
are connected to the present

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:48.120
There's no need to fear

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:55.760
I'll keep telling you that you're not alone

00:01:56.630 --> 00:02:01.900
The passionate emotions in your heart

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:07.540
Streak to the infinite future

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:13.130
Dreams surpass their limits

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:21.050
And will lead you to a bright place

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:53.050
WRGP Begins
Team 5D's vs Team Unicorn

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.370
It's finally starting.

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:06.970
Let's hope they complete the giant 
Circuit, just as Jose predicts.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:13.200
Neo Domino City is more excited 
than during the Fortune Cup!

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.290
To commemorate this first tournament, 
it's taking place at Moment's birthplace!

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:30.280
Block A preliminaries will be held at 
Memorial Circuit, the site of the Fortune Cup.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.980
The first match is incredible 
for the preliminaries!

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:38.920
Team Unicorn conquered the Atlantis Cup!  
The three members are Breo, Andore and Jean!

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:43.240
Facing them are Fortune 
Cup winner Yusei Fudo,

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:49.160
former King Jack Atlas and Aki 
Izayoi!  They're Team 5D's!

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:54.920
Two tournament favorites 
clash on the first day!

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:57.740
Who would have expected this?

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.130
Andore is going first.

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:08.920
Yusei, you're going first, right?

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:14.390
No.  Jack is first, Aki 
is second and I'm last.

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:17.240
Yusei, you're not first?

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:22.030
I thought you were going to 
settle things from practice.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.600
It's strategy.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:29.070
Only Jack's deck has the power 
to face Andore's power deck.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:34.480
I'll use my Red Dragon Archfiend 
to destroy that weak power deck!

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.160
What do you want?

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:49.960
Don't misunderstand.

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:51.660
I only came to say hello.

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:53.360
Too bad about that injury.

00:04:55.780 --> 00:04:59.070
But Team 5D's is still powerful without me!

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:05.370
I know.  We think you're our 
greatest rivals in this tournament.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.410
It's finally time to settle things.

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:12.610
Yeah.  Let's both give it our all today.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:14.960
Of course.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.320
But the battle has already begun.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:25.420
What's up with him?  He's cool-headed today!

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:27.430
He's totally different than before.

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:31.640
They finally realized how powerful we are.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:36.670
But as long as Jack Atlas is the first 
wheeler, everyone knows who'll win!

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:41.210
They completely fell for it.

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:46.600
Just as we expected, they chose 
Jack Atlas to be the first wheeler.

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:49.760
Everything is proceeding as planned.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:52.890
Andore, don't forget to 
use that at the start.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:54.550
I know.

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.110
It's almost time for this featured battle!

00:05:58.110 --> 00:06:01.830
The crews have returned to their 
pits, so the duel is about to begin!

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:07.790
It's finally starting.

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:11.040
Yeah.  This is the first 
step towards our dream.

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:14.700
I was looking forward to battling you.

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:18.740
We'll determine whose power deck is stronger!

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:23.220
Speed World 2 set!

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:36.890
Riding Duel!  Acceleration!

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:40.030
Both start simultaneously!

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.670
When it comes to acceleration, I can't lose!

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:48.170
I'm going to use my secret weapon.

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:54.810
What?

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:58.220
That's...

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:01.190
Overboost System!

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:05.100
Good.

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:10.790
Overboost System?

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:14.410
Yeah.  It's not against the regulation rules.

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:17.740
But that system is a double-edged sword.

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:22.770
It provides incredible acceleration, but 
it limits the maximum speed afterwards.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:24.800
It doesn't matter.

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:29.480
If we get to go first in tomorrow's 
duel, the battle is half over.

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:32.580
What?  Are we going to do Operation D?

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:34.550
Yeah, that's the plan.

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:39.560
Operation D is a secret strategy that 
we haven't used in any tournament.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:43.160
Team 5D's is a new team, but 
they have infinite potential.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:47.260
But they don't understand 
how to battle as a team.

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:49.880
That's where we have the advantage.

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:57.080
Jack Atlas, WRGP isn't a 
battle between individuals.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:08:00.410
I'll teach you how to battle as a team.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:03.610
If you want to go first 
that badly, I'll let you!

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:06.560
We now know who goes first 
and who goes second!

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:08.900
Start the duel!

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:13.490
Duel!

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:17.000
My turn!

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:20.250
I summon the Tuner Monster 
Uni-Horned Familiar!

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:30.550
I remove a spell card in my hand from 
play to Special Summon Monoceros!

00:08:34.940 --> 00:08:40.180
I can Special Summon Monoceros from my hand 
when I remove a spell card in my hand from play.

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:42.150
He's already planning to Synchro Summon!

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:44.850
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:08:49.240 --> 00:08:50.260
Strange.

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:52.940
What's wrong, Yusei?

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:55.230
Why didn't he Synchro Summon?

00:08:55.600 --> 00:09:02.470
If he's worried about Jack's attack power, 
he would want two monsters in defense position.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:06.440
But he Special Summoned Monoceros.

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:08.670
If he Synchro Summons Monoceros

00:09:08.670 --> 00:09:12.490
with a Beast-Type monster, he can 
resurrect the Beast-Type Tuner Monster.

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:16.450
Even if he Synchro Summoned, he would 
still have two monsters on his field.

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:20.420
In fact, his defense would be 
stronger if he Synchro Summoned.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:22.020
I see.

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.610
So why didn't he?

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:24.390
I don't know.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:28.090
But I have a bad feeling about this duel.

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:36.600
Here I go!  I'll show you my power!

00:09:37.030 --> 00:09:38.680
My turn!

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:45.280
I can Special Summon this card from my hand 
when monsters are only on your side of the field.

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:47.210
Appear, Vice Dragon!

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:56.790
But when I use this effect to Special Summon 
it, its attack and defense points are halved!

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:59.960
Then I summon Dark Resonator!

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:08.980
Level 3 Dark Resonator 
tunes Level 5 Vice Dragon!

00:10:12.490 --> 00:10:15.360
The pulse of the King now forms a line here!

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:17.770
Witness the power of the rumbling heavens!

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:20.080
Synchro Summon!

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:23.540
My soul!  Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:29.260
Jack Atlas already summoned 
Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:33.640
Show us the overwhelming power that 
we saw during the Fortune Cup!

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:34.930
Master Atlas!

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:38.350
When Red Dragon Archfiend attacks 
a monster in defense position,

00:10:38.350 --> 00:10:41.000
all your monsters in defense 
position are destroyed!

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:45.310
No matter how many defending monsters you 
have, it's pointless against Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:46.670
Go, Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:49.140
Absolute Powerforce!

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:50.840
He already fell for it.

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:54.310
I activate Uni-Horned Familiar's effect!

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:57.850
When Uni-Horned Familiar is attacked 
while in defense position...

00:10:57.850 --> 00:11:03.020
I can remove a monster on my field from play 
to remove Uni-Horned Familiar from play!

00:11:03.390 --> 00:11:04.350
What?

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:06.820
His field is now wide open!

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:11.240
I see!  He's trying to trap me!

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:16.800
Since the situation has changed, I 
stop Red Dragon Archfiend's attack!

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:19.240
Too bad, but that's not possible.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:23.000
Due to Uni-Horned Familiar's effect, 
you can't stop your attack!

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.210
What?

00:11:24.730 --> 00:11:26.870
Come, Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:32.350
Jack Atlas, taste your own power!

00:11:32.780 --> 00:11:35.550
I activate the trap Different 
Dimension Barrier - Lost Force!

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:41.520
When my monster leaves the field outside of 
battle, your monster's attack deflects back to you!

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:42.720
What?

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:54.540
Jack!

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:55.550
Jack!

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:56.410
Master Atlas!

00:11:56.410 --> 00:11:57.000
Jack!

00:11:58.230 --> 00:11:59.970
How dare you!

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:17.990
Whoa!  Jack Atlas was countered and 
took a whopping 3000 points of damage!

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:25.230
I set three cards and end my turn!

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:29.150
Jean, your strategy is perfect!

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:35.340
The moment Jack became the first wheeler 
and Andore managed to go first...

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:38.310
...Jack was guaranteed to take this damage.

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:41.010
I'll keep pressuring him 
while he's flustered.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:43.530
My turn!

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:49.690
Uni-Horned Familiar, whose effect 
removed it from play, returns!

00:12:49.690 --> 00:12:51.930
Appear, Uni-Horned Familiar!

00:12:57.660 --> 00:13:00.750
I can't Normal Summon D.D. Unicorn Knight...

00:13:00.750 --> 00:13:04.840
...but I can Special Summon it by 
resurrecting Monoceros that was removed from play.

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:07.220
Resurrect, Monoceros!

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:13.910
Appear, D.D. Unicorn Knight!

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:23.620
Level 2 Uni-Horned Familiar 
tunes Level 3 Monoceros!

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:31.960
Soaring thunder, merge with the ferocious 
wind to emerge from the world of illusions!

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:33.400
Synchro Summon!

00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:36.940
Neigh, Thunder Unicorn!

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:40.860
Thunder Unicorn has 2200 attack points!

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:43.170
It's weaker than my Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:50.400
Once per turn, your monster 
loses 500 attack points

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:54.150
for every non-Thunder Unicorn 
monster on my field.

00:13:54.590 --> 00:13:57.240
But I'll still have 2500 attack points.

00:13:57.240 --> 00:13:59.620
Red Dragon Archfiend won't 
lose to the likes of you!

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:03.090
You forgot about this effect!

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:05.560
I activate Monoceros's 
effect from my graveyard!

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:09.870
When Monoceros and a Beast-Type Tuner 
Monster are used to Synchro Summon,

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:12.030
the Tuner Monster resurrects!

00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:14.640
Resurrect, Uni-Horned Familiar!

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:21.440
There are now two non-Thunder 
Unicorn monsters on my field.

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:27.180
Red Dragon Archfiend's attack 
points decrease to 2000!

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:29.550
What?

00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:32.620
Go, Thunder Unicorn!

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:33.720
Thunder Spear!

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:46.470
How could Red Dragon Archfiend 
be destroyed so easily?

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:47.720
Master Atlas!

00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:48.600
Jack!

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:51.940
You guys worry about something else!

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:55.470
Aren't you supposed to 
be on patrol right now?

00:14:55.470 --> 00:14:58.290
You two should go back to your jobs!

00:14:58.290 --> 00:14:59.370
Who are you?

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:03.640
Andore is amazing.

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:08.590
Though he's using a complicated deck, 
he hasn't made a single mistake.

00:15:08.590 --> 00:15:11.980
I told you that he's a card-playing genius.

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:14.630
He instinctively feels the flow of a game.

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:21.600
His Removal Synchro Deck maximizes 
Andore's card-playing instincts.

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:24.120
Scary.

00:15:24.120 --> 00:15:26.570
I'm glad he's not our opponent.

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:31.280
Yusei, look at this!

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:32.270
What is it?

00:15:32.270 --> 00:15:34.750
Something entered the air intake.

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:37.520
Should he make a pit stop?

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:40.090
It means we'll have less 
Speed Counters than them.

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:41.640
Safety first.

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:42.990
Jack should make a pit stop.

00:15:43.360 --> 00:15:45.960
I set one card and end my turn.

00:15:46.270 --> 00:15:48.940
Enough with your stupid tricks!

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:53.130
You'll stop stealing my power when I 
acquire power that you can't steal!

00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:59.940
Unbelievable!  You want 
me to make a pit stop now?

00:15:59.940 --> 00:16:01.120
You must be kidding!

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:02.810
I'm continuing this duel!

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:05.260
My turn!

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:09.920
Jack is continuing to duel!

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:12.120
I summon Mad Archfiend!

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:20.090
Then I activate the trap Powerful Rebirth!

00:16:20.090 --> 00:16:24.600
I Special Summon a Level 4-or-below monster 
from my graveyard and equip it with this card.

00:16:24.600 --> 00:16:29.800
The equipped monster gains 100 attack 
and defense points and one Level.

00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:34.330
I Special Summon Dark 
Resonator from my graveyard!

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:43.150
I activate another trap!  Rage Resynchro!

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:47.880
By sending Synchro Material 
Monsters to the graveyard...

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:53.120
I can Special Summon its Synchro Monster from 
the graveyard with 500 additional attack points!

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:59.230
Level 4 Dark Resonator tunes Level 4 Mad 
Archfiend by sending them to the graveyard!

00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:02.030
The pulse of the King now forms a line here!

00:17:02.030 --> 00:17:04.530
Witness the power of the rumbling heavens!

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:06.300
Synchro Summon!

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:09.710
Resurrect, Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:12.510
3500 attack points?

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:14.980
Go, Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:17.680
Absolute Powerforce!

00:17:18.110 --> 00:17:20.380
I activate the trap Dimension Trap.

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:25.080
By removing a monster on my field and 
a trap card in my graveyard from play,

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:27.520
I can activate that trap's effect!

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:28.720
What?

00:17:29.050 --> 00:17:33.000
I remove Uni-Horned Familiar and Different 
Dimension Barrier - Lost Force from play!

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:36.970
Lost Force's effect is now on my field!

00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:43.940
Lost Force negates your attack, and you 
take damage equal to its attack points!

00:17:44.670 --> 00:17:47.140
This is bad!  Stop the attack, Jack!

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:49.340
If you take this, you'll lose!

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:56.420
If you think you can stop 
my attack, then try!

00:17:56.780 --> 00:17:58.890
I activate the trap Overpower!

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:05.590
This card negates and destroys the card 
that tries to stop a monster's attack!

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:13.560
Go, Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:16.340
Absolute Powerforce!

00:18:25.640 --> 00:18:26.680
Well done.

00:18:26.680 --> 00:18:29.190
He counterattacked from that situation?

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:32.750
Jack Atlas is a beast.

00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:36.220
He survived this turn.

00:18:37.270 --> 00:18:41.190
We've overlooked something 
that's strategically important.

00:18:41.780 --> 00:18:43.710
What do you mean, Yusei?

00:18:43.710 --> 00:18:46.430
His deck isn't a power deck.

00:18:46.860 --> 00:18:51.940
It's a deck that counteracts 
Jack's power deck.

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:53.470
That means back then...

00:19:01.340 --> 00:19:04.650
The deck he used wasn't his real deck?

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:09.690
But the battle has already begun.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:15.530
We completely fell for their trick.

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:17.500
What do you mean, Yusei?

00:19:17.770 --> 00:19:22.470
It wasn't coincidence that they 
challenged us during practice.

00:19:22.880 --> 00:19:26.870
What?  He deliberately fell in front of me?

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:29.310
Yes, to give us the wrong idea.

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:31.010
Give us the wrong idea?

00:19:31.290 --> 00:19:36.980
They made us think that Andore will be the 
first wheeler and that he would use a power deck.

00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:42.450
In order to face power with power, we 
chose Jack to be our first wheeler.

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:49.000
I see!  Team Unicorn did whatever it 
took to go first so that they could

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:51.330
set a trap against a power deck.

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:57.030
Team Unicorn has predicted 
everything that's happened so far?

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:07.560
They've figured out our plan.

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:10.430
But it's too late.

00:20:10.430 --> 00:20:12.980
Jack Atlas will lose.

00:20:13.280 --> 00:20:15.000
Jack, that was impressive.

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:17.400
You counterattacked from that situation.

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:22.230
But with your simple-minded dueling 
style, you can't win the WRGP.

00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:26.700
Be quiet!  I don't need you 
to lecture me about dueling!

00:20:27.340 --> 00:20:29.300
I expected that attack.

00:20:30.110 --> 00:20:31.300
What?

00:20:31.770 --> 00:20:34.500
Thanks to you, the battle is over.

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:37.970
I activate the trap card Parallel Selection!

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:45.980
When a Synchro Monster is destroyed, I can add 
one card that was removed from play to my hand.

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:50.690
I'm bringing back Speed 
Spell - End of the Storm.

00:20:50.690 --> 00:20:51.650
What?

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:52.620
This is bad!

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:54.810
My turn!

00:20:56.090 --> 00:20:59.290
Jack Atlas only has 800 life points.

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:02.360
And Andore has four Speed Counters this turn.

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:05.920
I activate Speed World 2's effect!

00:21:05.920 --> 00:21:08.620
By removing four Speed Counters,

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:13.910
you take 800 points of damage for 
every Speed Spell in my hand!

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:18.890
You lose, Jack Atlas.

00:21:32.860 --> 00:21:33.530
What?

00:22:08.360 --> 00:22:13.350
The small cliff floats on the Milky Way

00:22:13.350 --> 00:22:18.230
The sights I see are different 
than what I imagined

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:23.170
Were you able to move on from the past?

00:22:23.170 --> 00:22:28.180
The answer isn't no, but 
there's something missing

00:22:28.180 --> 00:22:33.230
The cruel god tests us

00:22:33.230 --> 00:22:39.790
Let's fill the emptiness 
and head to the next stage

00:22:39.790 --> 00:22:43.860
If you ask me "What's our relationship?"

00:22:43.860 --> 00:22:49.700
We're more than friends... 
but that's not quite right

00:22:49.700 --> 00:22:53.790
Bond is the proper word

00:22:53.790 --> 00:22:59.410
As we fight, we understand each other

00:22:59.410 --> 00:23:02.590
"Where are you right now?"  "On Earth"

00:23:02.590 --> 00:23:04.850
Because I'm not an astronaut

00:23:04.850 --> 00:23:09.380
I have no problems when 
I'm below the ozone layer

00:23:09.380 --> 00:23:12.350
"I know, I'm coming right away."

00:23:12.350 --> 00:23:15.790
You want to party until the morning

00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:19.170
At our special place
